1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wallace E. LeLand, 91, of Cheyenne, Wyo, passed away at his home Wednesday evening, June 18, 2014, surrounded by his loving family.
2 CONT
2 CONT LeLand was born Sept.3, 1922, in Bricelyn, a son of the late John J. and Josephine (Johnson) LeLand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wallace served in the European Theatre for the United States Army during world War 11. Following his honorable discharge, he owned and operated a Standard Oil Station and later worked as an insurance agent for Modern Woodmen. His 
2 CONC many interests included fishing in northern Minnesota and playing his guitar. He also enjoyed his service as the Bricelyn Fire and Rescue Chief, having directed and participated in over 100 rescue missions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wallace is survived by 4 children (3 of whom are Doctors); 6 grandchildren, 8 great grandchildren and 2 brothers and his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is preceded in death by his parents, six brothers and four sisters.
